  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nA full break down of the trough continues to trend by Saturday\nwith most models agreeing to a new upper-level ridge slowly\nbuilding into an upper-level high pressure system across the\nWestern United States this weekend. With the high building, most\nmodels see the Panhandles returning to much drier conditions with\nchances of precipitation dropping below 10 percent for both days.\nThis pattern looks to continue into next week with present model\nagreement seeing the high hold through Monday. By Tuesday, models\ndo suggest that high can break down in favor or a weak trough\npushing through. However, chances of precipitation are not looking\ntoo great with current ensembles only giving us around 10 to 15\npercent chance that evening. Regardless this system looks to be\nshort lived with most models seeing a new ridge build in by\nWednesday. As for temperatures, cooler weather does look to hold\nfor at least one more day with Saturday seeing highs in the mid to\nupper 70s and lows in the mid 40s to low 50s that morning. Beyond\nthat, however, a warming trend does look to follow with afternoon\nhighs heating back into the mid to upper 80s for the middle of\nnext week.",
